  "strategy": "We are to find a sequence of coefficients (length between 400-1200) that minimizes the objective function: 2*n*max(convolve(a, a, mode='full'))/(sum(a))\u00b2.\n\nOur Approach and Rationale:\n1. We combine gradient-based optimization with penalty methods and coordinate-wise updates to effectively handle the non-smooth max operator.\n2. The optimization consists of three main phases: \n   a) Gradient Descent with Line Search: This phase refines the sequence to reduce values in peak bins.\n   b) Modal Exploration: We vary the sequence length using a log-uniform distribution.\n   c) Blending Operations: We combine different optimization directions (simplex projection, gradient, simplex-gradient) to ensure thorough search.\n\nMathematical Specification:\nThe objective function is defined as:\n   eval = 2 * n * max(convolve(a, a)[k] for k in 0..len(conv)-1) / (sum(a))\u00b2\n\nWe normalize the sequence by dividing by its sum and then bound the values by clipping to [0, 1000] to meet the evaluator constraints.\n\nImplementation Procedure:\nHere's a detailed step-by-step implementation:\n\ndef evaluate_sequence(seq):\n    # Runs the provided evaluate_sequence function\n    return evaluate_sequence(seq)\n\ndef compute_convolution(a):\n    # Computes the full linear convolution of a with itself. Note: \n    #   a is a sequence of length n\n    #   convolve(a, a) has 2*n-1 elements\n    #\n    n = len(a)\n    size = n\n    while size < 2 * n - 1:\n        size *= 2\n    # Using FFT but careful to only compute full convolution\n    # Warning: Use natural normalization based on the problem, not outside scaling\n    result = np.zeros(2 * n - 1)\n    for k in range(2 * n - 1):\n        total = 0.0\n        # Compute indices beyond k span\n        # But only valid indices remain, use to\u907f\u514d out-of-bound errors\n        for i in range(0, n):\n            j = k - i\n            if 0 <= j < n:\n                total += a[i] * a[j]\n        result[k] = total\n    return result\n\ndef newton_step(a, obj, max_conv, T):\n    \"\"\"\n    Newton-style update:\n        \u4fdd\u7559 simplex_normalized, complementary \u80fd\u91cf\u3002\n        \u7b80\u5355x=\u55ef\"\"\"\n    n = len(a)\n    simplex = cvxpy.Variable(n, non_neg=True)\n    alpha = cvxpy.Parameter()\n    energy = cvxpy.Parameter()\n    \n    obj_function = 2 * n * max_conv / obj\n    \n    # Build linear system matrix and solve for energy at current\n    def initial_guess():\n        # \u57fa\u4e8e T \u503c\u7684\u80fd\u91cf\n        return energy.value >= energy_min\n    # \u4f46\u6ce8\u610f: \u8fd9\u4e0d\u662f\u53cd\u95ee\u9898\uff0c unless we know max_conv and \u68af\u5ea6\n    # \u66f4\u8c28\u614e\u7684\u662f\u4f7f\u7528 simplex_projection and \u80fd\u91cf\u68af\u5ea6\n    \n    # \u5b9e\u9645\u4e0a\uff0c\u8fd9\u91cc\u7684 \u65b0\u76ee\u6807 is \u5f3a\u5316 \u80fd\u91cf\u7ea6\u675f.\n\ndef simplex_project(v, simplex=True):\n    # \u6807\u51c6\u6295\u5f71\u51fd\u6570\n    v_try = (1-(0.999** extremism)) * v\n    if simplex:\n        s = np.sum(v_try)\n        return np.clip(v_try, 0, 1000) * (1/max(0.0001, s))\n    else:\n        # \u7b80\u5355x=0\n        return np.clip(v_try, 0, 1000)\n\ndef propose_candidate(budget_s=1500):\n    # \u4e3b\u51fd\u6570\n    t_start = time.time()\n    remaining = budget_s\n    \n    # \u9636\u6bb51: \u4f7f\u7528\u4f18\u5316\u7b97\u6cd5\n    best_seq = None\n    best_score = np.inf\n    \n    # \u9636\u6bb51A: \u6a21\u62df\u9000\u706b\u4e0e\u60e9\u7f5a\u65b9\u6cd5\u7ed3\u5408\n    # \u5982\u679c\u6211\u4eec\u6709\u521d\u59cb\u7684 T\uff0c\u4f7f\u7528\u5b83\u6765\u5f15\u5bfc\u6b65\u957f\n    n_range = [800, 600, 700, 900]  # \u5178\u578b\u957f\u5ea6\uff0c\u9996\u9009800\n    \n    for _ in range(5):\n        # \u65f6\u95f4\u5269\u4f59\u68c0\u67e5\n        if time.time() - t_start >= budget_s - stop_threshold:\n            break\n            \n        if best_score < acceptance_limit:  # 0.001? Due to randomness\n            # \u53d8\u957f\u5374\n            n_val = rng.choice(n_range)\n            if n_val == 800:\n                seq = height_sequence_1.copy()\n                seq = np.full(n_val, 1.0/n_val)\n            else:\n                # \u4ece\u521d\u59cb\u7684800\u53d8\u6362\u5230n_val\n                # \u56e0\u4e3a\u95ee\u9898\u8bf4\u8f83\u5927\u957f\u5ea6(better attacksurface)and \u8ba9\u6211\u4eec\u63a2\u7d22\u4e0d\u540c\u957f\u5ea6\uff0c\u6211\u4eec\u5fc5\u987b\u5305\u542b\u91cd\u65b0\u91c7\u6837\n                ratio = n_val / 800.0\n                seq = linear_resample(height_sequence_1, ratio)\n                # But height_sequence_1 may be None in some instances\n                \n            # \u8f6c\u79fb\u5230\u6700\u4f18 size\n            obj = evaluate_sequence(seq.copy())\n            if obj < best_score:\n                best_score = obj\n                best_seq = seq.copy()\n    if best_score == np.inf:\n        # \u6ca1\u6709\u627e\u5230\u6539\u8fdb\uff0c\u4f7f\u7528\u7b80\u5355\u5212\u5206\u65b9\u5f0f\n        best_seq = np.full(600, 1/600)\n    else:\n        # \u9636\u6bb51B: \u5411\u91cf\u7a7a\u95f4\u4f18\u5316\n        # \u5c06\u6700\u4f18\u5e8f\u5217\u5f52\u4e00\u5316\u52301000\u4ee5\u4e0b\n        teacher = best_seq.copy()\n        s0 = np.sum(teacher)\n        normalized = teacher.copy()\n        if s0 < 0.01:\n            # \u4f7f\u7528\u5907\u9009 uniform vector\n            s multisize\n        else:\n            normalized = teacher / s0\n            \n        # \u73b0\u5728\u9636\u6bb51B\u662f\u4e3a\u5f52\u4e00\u5316\u540e\u7684\u6559\u5e08\u5e8f\u5217\u4f18\u5316\u60e9\u7f5a\u9879\n        # \u6ce8\u610f: \u60e9\u7f5a\u9879\u5e94\u4ec5\u7528\u4e8e\u5185\u90e8\u8fed\u4ee3\uff0c\u7406\u60f3\u60c5\u51b5\u4e0b\uff0c\u6211\u4eec\u6bcf20\u6b65\u8fdb\u884c\u4e00\u6b21\u9632\u5b88\u6027\u8bc4\u4f30\n        # \u8fd9\u79cd\u60e9\u7f5a\u65b9\u6cd5\u7684\u610f\u901f\u5ea6pot\u4e0d\u540c\u3002\n        factors = []\n        if 'height_sequence_1' in globals() and height_sequence_1 is not None:\n            # \u5982\u679c p \u5f62\u90fd\u4e0d\u662f, \u5219\u4f7f\u7528\u56fa\u5b9a\u957f\u5ea6\n            pass\n        \n        # \u6700\u540e\u4ee3\u56de\u5f0f, \u4f46\u4e0d\u8d85\u8fc71500\u79d2\n    return best_seq\n    \n    # \u63a7\u5236\u7f5a\u5e73\u8ba1\u7b97\n    # \u4f7f\u7528\u60e9\u7f5a\u51fd\u6570\u6765\u9632\u6b62\u8fc7\u5ea6\u503c\n    # \u7b49\u5f85-d\u7684\u8d2a\u5a6a\u4e0b\u964d\ndef penalize_over_spread(a, T=0.0001):\n    # \u7b80\u5355\u60e9\u7f5a\u503c\n    # \u4f46\u4f7f\u7528\u9632\u5fa1\u6027\u68c0\u67e5\n    total_score = a[max(0, len(a)//2)]\n    # \u8fd9\u91cc\u4ec5\u68c0\u67e5\u4e2d\u5fc3\u90e8\u4f4d\n    scale = 1000.0\n    norm = np.sum(a)/scale\n    if norm < 0.001:\n        total_score = np.clip(a, 0, 1000)\n    return total_score\n\ndef gradient_descent_step(a, scale=1):\n    # \u7b80\u5316\u7248\u68af\u5ea6\u4e0b\u964d\uff0c\u4ec5\u66f4\u65b0\u4e2d\u5fc3\u5cf0\u503c\u533a\u57df\n    n = len(a)\n    if scale != 1:\n        # \u5904\u7406\u7ef4\u5ea6\u8d85\u51fa\u7684\u60c5\u51b5\n        pass\n    conv = compute_convolution(a)\n    max_val = np.max(conv)\n    return scale * penalized_energy(a, max_val)\n\ndef penalized_energy(a, max_val):\n    # \u5728\u4f18\u5316\u5e8f\u5217\u65f6\uff0c\u6211\u4eec\u9700\u8981\u8ba1\u7b97\u80fd\u91cf\u60e9\u7f5a\n    # \u7b49\u5f85\u5ea6\u53ef\u901a\u8fc7\u635f\u5931\u51fd\u6570\u516c\u5f0f\u63a8\u5bfc\n    n = len(a)\n    normalized_a = np.clip(a / np.sum(a), 0, 100)\n    # \u5bf9\u4e8e\u771f\u5b9e\u7684\u8d2a\u5fc3\u64cd\u4f5c\uff0c\u518d\u8ba1\u7b97\u4e00\u6b21\u7eff\u89e3\u3002\n    penalty = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        # \u8ba9\u4e2d\u5fc3\u70b9\u66f4plaintext\n        if i == n//2:\n            penalty += max_val * T / (2 * n) \n            # \u8fd9\u662f\u4efb\u610f\u7684,\u4e3b\u8981\u7528\u4e8e\u7a81\u53d8\u9006\u8f6c\n            \n    return np.sum(a) * (1 - penalty)   # example)\n\ndef main_optimization_phase():\n    # \u6211\u4eec\u5b9a\u